@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# The Daily Grind
+
+Start the static site with `pnpm start`. Run automated tests with `npm test` (Node.js 18 or newer).
+
+## WebMCP
+
+The page progressively registers three client-side tools using `document.modelContext.registerTool`:
+
+| Tool | Behavior |
+| --- | --- |
+| `get_seasonal_favorites` | Returns the displayed drink names, descriptions, and detail links. Accepts `{}`. |
+| `get_site_navigation` | Returns the linked page labels, paths, and absolute URLs. Accepts `{}`. |
+| `navigate_to_page` | Opens a listed path in the current tab. Accepts, for example, `{"path":"/order-online"}`. |
+
+Read tools use the current DOM as their source. Navigation accepts only explicitly allowed paths that are also linked on the page. Logout remains a manual action. Opening the ordering page does not place an order. The destination pages are existing links; this static repository does not implement those routes.
+
+Tools require a secure context (HTTPS or trustworthy localhost) and a browser with WebMCP enabled. Unsupported browsers retain the existing page and links. Registrations use an AbortSignal for cleanup on `pagehide` and are restored on `pageshow`, including back/forward cache restoration. Registration failures clean up partial registrations and log a warning without affecting the page.
+
+WebMCP is experimental. See the current [Chrome setup instructions](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp#get-started), [imperative API documentation](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/imperative-api), and [specification](https://webmachinelearning.github.io/webmcp/). No backend MCP server, API key, or transport is needed.
+
+The Node test suite invokes registered tools against a simulated browser environment using the actual HTML content. It covers tool results, input validation, navigation restrictions, unsupported contexts, lifecycle cleanup/restoration, and registration failures. It does not verify a native browser's WebMCP implementation.
